[00:08.11]A: I used to rule the world
[00:11.80]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:14.28]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:18.60]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:35.59]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:39.65]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:42.91]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:46.72]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:49.56]A: One minute I held the key
[00:53.53]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:56.20]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:00.46]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:04.28]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:08.16]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:11.62]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:14.74]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:18.54]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:21.94]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:24.57]A: Never an honest word
[01:28.28]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:44.93]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:49.10]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:51.79]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:56.15]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[01:59.34]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:03.18]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:05.63]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:10.20]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:13.97]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:17.57]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:20.98]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:24.44]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:27.92]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:31.50]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:34.69]A: Never an honest word
[02:37.76]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:10.10]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:13.15]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:16.73]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:20.01]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:23.63]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:27.09]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[03:30.23]A: Never an honest word
[03:33.47]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
